error[E0835]: cannot give away `account` — it's borrowed, not owned
  --> docs/book/errors/passing-values/consume_borrowed.rk:15:22
    |
 14 | func describe(account: Account) -> i64 {
    |               ------- `account` is declared as a borrowed parameter
 15 |     return close_out(account)
    |                      ^^^^^^^ `close_out` takes ownership, and `account` isn't yours to give
    = fix: take it: `take account: …` in the signature — then the caller can see
          it goes
    = why: the caller keeps a parameter it didn't mark `take` and goes on using
          it, so consuming it here would leave them holding something that's
          gone. For a `@resource` that's a second close of a real handle.
          [mem.parameters/PM1, mem.linear/L1]
